package PumpModes "The four ways of specifying a centrifugal pump's duty, on one feed"
  extends Modelica.Icons.ExamplesPackage;
  annotation(
    Documentation(info = "<html><head></head><body><div>Four flowsheets, identical apart from how the pump's duty is specified. All four pump the same feed to the same outlet pressure, so <b>they must all return the same answer</b> — that is what makes this package a test rather than a demonstration.</div><div><br></div><div><b>The feed</b> (every model): pure water, 100 mol/s, 101325 Pa, 300 K. Raoult's law. The pump runs at 75% efficiency and raises the stream to 5 bar.</div><div><br></div><div><b>The four models:</b></div><div><ol><li><a href=\"modelica://PumpModes.SpecFlowsheetEquation\">SpecFlowsheetEquation</a> — the original library style: the pump is left one equation short and the flowsheet closes it with <code>B1.Pdel = 398675;</code></li><li><a href=\"modelica://PumpModes.SpecOutletPressure\">SpecOutletPressure</a> — <code>spec = OutletPressure</code>, <code>Pout_spec = 500000</code></li><li><a href=\"modelica://PumpModes.SpecPressureIncrease\">SpecPressureIncrease</a> — <code>spec = PressureIncrease</code>, <code>Pdel_spec = 398675</code></li><li><a href=\"modelica://PumpModes.SpecPowerRequired\">SpecPowerRequired</a> — <code>spec = PowerRequired</code>, <code>Q_spec = 961.6676</code></li></ol></div><div><b>Expected result</b>, common to all four:</div><div><br></div><div><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"4\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td><b>Outlet pressure</b></td><td>500000 Pa</td></tr><tr><td><b>Pressure increase</b></td><td>398675 Pa</td></tr><tr><td><b>Shaft power</b></td><td>961.668 W</td></tr><tr><td><b>Outlet temperature</b></td><td>300.1289 K</td></tr><tr><td><b>NPSH available</b></td><td>10.0133 m</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div><br></div><div>The fourth model is the interesting one: it is given <i>only</i> the shaft power and has to recover the pressure rise by inverting the energy balance. It agrees with the other three only because that balance retains the friction heat — see section 7 of the library's ATTRIBUTION.md.</div></body></html>"));
end PumpModes;
